WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.940
Listen up, everyone.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.820
I just got a call from Satou's mother.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:14.450
Apparently, he's quitting the Dolphins 
because they're moving to Gunma.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.600
It's unfortunate, but that's how it is.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.330
I've been asked to pass on his regards.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.180
<i>This can't be real.</i>

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.060
<i>It can't. It can't!</i>

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.690
<i>Hikaru can't move away.</i>

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.710
<i>He can't quit the Dolphins!</i>

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.690
<i>It's not happening!</i>

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:22.160
Some Day, For Sure

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.870
<i>Please answer, Hikaru.</i>

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:30.360
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.400
Hey, kid!

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.880
Do you live here?

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.670
Did you lock yourself out?

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.510
N-No, my friend lives here.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.260
I'm trying to get in touch with 
Satou-kun in apartment 1501.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.260
1501, huh?

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.060
Oh!

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:50.190
The family in that unit moved out yesterday.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.310
A mother and her boy, right?

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:02.820
What?

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.530
I'm in the middle of changing!

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.460
How many times do I have to tell you not 
to come in here when I'm using the bath?!

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.200
Hey, are you listening?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.130
Oh, sorry. I didn't realize you were in here.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.800
Mom!

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.180
What's wrong with Daigo? He's acting funny.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.440
Well, you see...

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.440
What? Hikaru-kun moved to Gunma?

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:38.540
Yes.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.470
But why?

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.760
He only just moved here from the States.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.740
I don't know all the particulars,

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:53.870
but the mom of one of his classmates said
that his mom said her goodbyes last Friday.

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:58.880
But it looks like Daigo only heard 
about it today from his coach.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.630
What? That's so awful!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:05.590
But I don't get it. Hikaru-kun's dad 
has been seeing Daigo on a daily basis.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.620
Why didn't he say something?

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.010
He probably didn't know.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.770
Toshi-kun got divorced several years ago.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.860
And, even though his 
mother has sole custody,

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.860
when Toshi-kun was playing 
in the major leagues,

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.740
they lived in America so Hikaru-kun 
could see his father every month.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.760
So that's what happened.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.720
I think his mother's originally from Gunma.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:35.460
She probably decided to
live closer to her parents.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.350
All of this must be a pretty 
big shock for Daigo.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.240
I wonder if he's okay.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.590
I'm worried about him, too.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:48.740
Having Hikaru-kun around reignited 
Daigo's passion for baseball.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.850
Shigeno-kun!

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.570
Is it true that Hikaru-kun has transferred?

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:06.070
I didn't see him on my way to school today, 
so I asked one of my friends in Class 4.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.280
They told me Friday was his last day!

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.410
Seems like it.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:14.410
I hadn't heard anything about it.
I was so shocked!

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:17.410
Did he say anything to you about it?

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:18.510
No.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.500
I only found out at practice on Saturday.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.500
Huh? R-Really?

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.010
Why would he even do that?

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:30.460
He wasn't here long, but I felt 
like we'd become good friends.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.020
I can't believe he didn't 
even say anything to you.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.340
Forget about it already.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.640
I mean, there was probably 
a reason for the rush.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.900
B-But he already knew about it Friday, 
so he could've said something...

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.570
I said, forget it!

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.050
Who cares? He's gone.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.740
Just stop talking about him.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:53.490
Next up, Group B.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.660
Wall handstands!

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.800
You, over there! Keep your knees flat.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.170
Don't splay your legs.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.420
<i>Who cares?</i>

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.170
Five more seconds.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.220
<i>Who the hell cares?</i>

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.800
<i>I can't wait to forget him.</i>

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:12.720
<i>I'll wipe him from my memory!</i>

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.790
Oh, Daigo, you're home.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:23.480
Welcome back.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.440
Yeah, I just got home.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:31.200
You're not going to the batting center today?

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:35.590
Isn't your coach, Toshi-kun, 
there on weekdays?

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:38.210
I called and canceled.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.080
I mean, I'm a right fielder.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:43.600
And I don't have a reason to
aim to be a catcher anymore.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:45.960
But...

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.380
Just drop it!

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.010
I guess I'll let him be for a while.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.020
Shigeno

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:59.650
I wonder if that's a delivery...

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.790
What? Huh? I-I don't...

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.780
U-Um, just one moment, please!

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:09.280
Huh?

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.060
Whose car is that?

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.910
We have visitors?

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:16.410
I'm home...

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:22.120
Mom... and Satou-san!

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.500
I-It's not what it looks like!
We were just...

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.800
Ah, I just remembered I needed 
something from the convenience store!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.340
Izumi!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.240
Here you go.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.370
Is this okay?

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.870
Thank you so much!

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.400
I'll treasure it forever and ever! 
A real pro's autograph!

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.710
Oh, but I'm not one anymore.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:46.090
Oh, yeah. Then, how about I call you "Dad"?

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:51.090
I already told you!
He was just helping me up!

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:53.730
It's okay, Mom, I get it.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.700
Satou-san's super cool and Pop's in Taiwan...

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.880
Stop it.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:00.180
Just get Daigo to come out here, will you?

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.490
Okay.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.200
I'm so sorry about this, Satou-san.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:11.340
You've gone to all this trouble to coach him,
and he just rings you and cancels...

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.750
It's fine.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:16.370
After all, my son's move to
 Gunma was very sudden.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.360
He's lost his baseball buddy,

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.880
so he's probably still getting
a handle on his emotions.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.270
Hey...

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.730
He says he doesn't want to see you.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:40.620
But he already knew about it Friday, 
so he could've said something...

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.800
We were playing catch that day.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.810
Why didn't he?!

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:46.840
Daigo-kun?

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:50.820
Wh-What are you doing here?

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.860
I told you I wasn't going to 
practice catching anymore, didn't I?

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:57.840
There's no point now that Hikaru's gone.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.100
I didn't come here to 
browbeat you into practicing.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.100
I just wanted to give you this.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.270
It's a letter for you from Hikaru.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:14.530
Dad, 
please give this
 to Daigo-kun 
without opening it

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.910
It arrived today.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.530
The envelope says to
hand it to you, unopened.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:16.610
From Hikaru?

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:27.500
I'll be off now.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.210
Oh?

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.670
I'll only bring the mood down if I stay.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.450
A-Ah, thank you for coming all 
this way to deliver it.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:39.590
Hey, hey, what does he say?
 Read it out loud, Daigo!

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:40.220
Izumi.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:46.880
<i>Daigo-kun...</i>

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.160
<i>I'm sorry I disappeared like that,</i>

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:52.820
<i>and I'm sorry I have to say 
my goodbyes in a letter.</i>

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:58.820
<i>I'm sure hearing that I'd moved
 to Gunma took you by surprise.</i>

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:03.580
<i>I don't think anybody was more 
surprised than I was, though.</i>

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:09.570
<i>We've moved to Gunma because my mother's
 from there, and my grandmother's not well.</i>

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.060
<i>The reason for moving was to be near to her.</i>

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:17.660
<i>I guess my mother was worried that 
I'd be dead against moving,</i>

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:20.300
<i>so she kept it a secret 
until the very last minute.</i>

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:25.930
<i>When she told me last Thursday, 
it was a bolt out of the blue.</i>

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:30.100
<i>I couldn't believe I had to leave behind 
all of my classmates, Sakura-san,</i>

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:34.780
<i>and most importantly, you, the guy 
who has quickly become my best friend.</i>

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:38.150
<i>It was an incredibly hard thing to do.</i>

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:45.220
<i>I knew I should have said goodbye 
to you that day, face to face,</i>

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.720
<i>but I couldn't bear the thought of our 
last game of catch ending in tears.</i>

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:53.500
<i>I just couldn't say it.</i>

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.010
<i>I'm so sorry, Daigo-kun.</i>

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.680
<i>I want to thank you for everything.</i>

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.880
<i>Thanks to you, I discovered
 how much I loved baseball.</i>

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:14.950
<i>Once my emotions are back in check,
I might play some baseball here, too.</i>

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:21.530
<i>My dream of having you catch 
my pitches didn't come true,</i>

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.660
<i>but if we both keep playing, I know 
we'll meet on the diamond again.</i>

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.160
<i>And...</i>

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:33.970
<i>Some day, for sure,
we're going to be an invincible battery!</i>

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:47.220
Mom! Mom!

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.480
Mom! Phone! Phone!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.100
I'm gonna practice catching after all, 
so ask him to come back!

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:53.600
What?!

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.070
Ringing

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.070
Shigeno 
Family

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:09.540
Hey, Daigo.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.630
Wanna come over today?

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.840
I got a new game.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.690
Sorry, but I already have plans.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:18.620
Oh, okay.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:20.220
Some other time, then.

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:20.840
Sure!

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:21.630
Later!

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:26.320
He looks so much happier today.

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.740
By "plans," does he mean...

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.680
Mifune
Batting Center

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.560
Fastballs

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:42.210
Okay!

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.570
Nice framing.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.610
You've gotten a lot better.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:50.220
130 kmph fastballs aren't
 scary anymore, huh?

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:55.200
Yeah, I can't believe I used to get 
freaked out by 120 kmph balls.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:57.820
This protective gear is starting 
to feel like decoration.

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:00.820
The trick to fastballs 
is getting used to them.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:03.670
Why don't we give 150 kmph a try?

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:08.120
I'm kidding.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.970
There's no reason to practice 
catching those at junior level.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:15.940
Mifune Batting Center

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:15.940
I think we've done all the catching 
practice we need to in this place.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:19.190
Mifune 
Batting Center

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.190
I want to start concentrating 
on other things.

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:23.080
Daigo-kun, think it'd be okay to do 
our sessions at your house from now on?

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:25.320
Yeah, sure, no problem.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.820
I knew it. He's back playing baseball.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.780
All right! I'll start playing again, too.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.530
Uh, sir?

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:37.000
Yeah?

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.150
I read Hikaru's letter,

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:43.000
and of course, I want to 
be a catcher at some point,

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.330
but for the upcoming tournament, 
I'm supposed to be playing right field.

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:48.680
I see.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.620
I don't have any problems catching fly balls.

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:56.180
The issue is getting the ball back home.

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:57.880
Throwing it, you mean?

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:03.700
That's a stumbling block in 
my quest to be a catcher, too.

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:05.030
Daigo-kun?

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.710
M-My arm's so weak, 
I can't even throw a ball 50 meters.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.740
Even though I'm the son 
of the great Shigeno Goro.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:16.640
I-It's laughable, isn't it?

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:19.520
I'm sorry for bringing it up at this stage.

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:23.800
I just don't have any talent.

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:26.260
I see.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:30.730
Well, I'd have to see for myself, 
but if you're a right fielder,

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:33.160
I guess we should practice 
throwing the ball back.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.580
O-Okay.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.670
Let me warn you about 
one thing though, Daigo-kun.

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:42.160
I never want to hear you say 
you don't have talent again.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.280
Maybe you can in ten years' time, but not now.

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:49.780
Yes, sir.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.460
Weren't we going to practice at my house?

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:06.380
Your backyard is too small for practicing 
right field stuff like long throws.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:07.880
Oh, right.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.380
Okay, let's see how good your arm is.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:19.580
I think this is about 50 meters.

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:22.730
Imagine you're throwing it from 
right field back to home base!

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.060
Uh, y-yessir!

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:27.760
<i>I wonder if I can do it...</i>

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.540
Looks like it got here, after all.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:41.160
Yeah, somehow.

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:44.170
The runner made it home, though.

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.600
Uh, I've only thrown one ball...

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:53.630
I don't need to see any more.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:57.190
Throwing long like that isn't 
good for a young person's arm.

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:57.970
And it's unnecessary.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:15:59.100
What?

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.540
Basically, you guys only need to be 
able to throw from home to second;

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.480
a distance of roughly 32 meters.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.270
Really?!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:11.550
Wait, have you always worried 
about how weak your arm is?

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.640
Y-Yes, actually.

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:18.340
It's neither a handicap
nor a cause for concern.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:22.100
Anybody can master throwing the ball 
through practice and technique.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.210
You can even make it look 
like you've got a strong arm.

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.750
Of course, there are actual 
monsters like your dad.

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:31.840
But they're in the minority.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:36.140
It's not as if I started out 
with a strong arm as a kid, either.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.240
Even after I went pro,

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:41.140
there were plenty of players 
who had a stronger arm than me.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:43.560
I-Is that really true?

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:45.040
Sure is.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:50.360
However, it's not going to be zero to 
laser beam in a week, or even a month.

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:55.110
It all depends how passionate you are,
and whether you put in the work daily.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:56.610
I'll give it my all!

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.720
Please train me hard!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.860
Bye.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.650
See you tomorrow!

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:08.840
This is so annoying.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:10.840
Dad! Mom! Please!

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.500
I really want to join the Dolphins!

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.220
This again?

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.100
What's all this about 
baseball all of a sudden?

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.340
Is this to do with some boy 
you like or something?

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.350
What?!

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.590
Of course not!

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:28.560
No matter what you say, I'm against the idea!

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.200
Hey, Sakura!

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:39.380
Are you busy right now?

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:41.190
Not really.

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:43.580
Will you come with me, then?

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:46.170
Huh?

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:54.050
<i>I figured it'd be something 
like this, but whatever.</i>

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.830
Satou-san has work,

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:00.790
so I was thinking I wouldn't 
get to play catch today,

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:03.260
but I'm glad you had nothing else to do.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:05.000
"Nothing else to do"?

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.890
That's kinda rude, isn't it?

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:13.740
Hey, Shigeno-kun, your throws aren't bad.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.990
Though, not as good as
Hikaru-kun's, obviously.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.930
Don't compare me to him.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:21.560
I've actually improved quite a bit.

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.410
All thanks to Satou-san.

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.640
Lucky you.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:31.420
Being taught by an ex-pro isn't the kind of
opportunity that comes along every day.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.090
What's that? You jelly?

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:35.560
Yes.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:39.510
To tell you the truth, 
I'd love to play baseball.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.340
And join the Dolphins.

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:42.540
What?!

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:46.850
What's so shocking about that?

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:49.440
My older brother was in the Dolphins,

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:52.400
so I've been cheering 
for him since I was small.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:56.360
And when I was Hikaru-kun's training partner,

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:59.570
I started having fun playing it, too.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:01.260
I see.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.030
Then, just do it.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.960
You think it's that easy?!

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:07.440
I've already asked my 
parents a bunch of times,

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:09.320
but they always say no!

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:10.830
Then, don't.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:11.790
Huh?

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:15.520
If you're going to give up the first time 
someone's against you doing it,

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:19.420
that just means baseball isn't 
all that important to you.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:23.680
Anyway, throw the ball here already!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.420
<i>How dare you?!</i>

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:29.430
<i>I still remember how much you 
moped and whined about baseball!</i>

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.230
You jackass!

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.010
Hey! Watch where you're throwing!

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:40.610
Hey! Don't just leave!

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:45.330
Jeez. What's <i>her</i> problem?

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:59.210
Mutsuko's had her nose 
to the grindstone recently.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:02.460
Your mother tells me you've 
been studying in the morning.

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:05.340
I decided to get up an hour 
early to do my schoolwork.

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:08.180
That way, playing baseball won't 
get in the way of my entrance exams.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.620
You're still going on about that?

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:14.990
Buying all the gear for it 
would be a real financial burden.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.650
We explained that to you before.

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:18.720
I don't need new equipment!

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:20.320
I'll just use my brother's old gear!

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:21.110
So...

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:23.740
No! Just give it up already!

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:30.890
If you're going to give up the first time 
someone's against you doing it,

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:34.500
that just means baseball isn't 
all that important to you.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:39.000
It's important to me.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.090
Did you know?

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:47.350
When you catch a ball, it makes 
a really satisfying "paff" sound.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:48.970
Mutsuko?

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:52.740
I'm still bad at catching, 
so when I play catch,

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:55.060
I'm always nervous that 
I might cut short that sound.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:58.340
"Next time, I'll make it 
last longer," I tell myself.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:02.820
That's why it makes me so happy 
when I get to hear that "paff."

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.740
Or when I manage a good throw!

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.620
Things I can't do now could 
become possible through my efforts.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:13.830
And that prospect excites me
like nothing else!

00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:16.080
I'll also study hard for my entrance exams.

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:19.450
I'll knuckle down and make sure I pass them!

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:22.590
So please, let me join the Dolphins!

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:26.590
I want to find out how much joy 
I can get out of baseball!

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:29.250
And I can't do that if 
I don't get serious about it!

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:39.440
I have an announcement to make 
before we start the session.

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:43.190
Next week, we're going to have 
a practice match against Minamigaoka.

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:47.940
It'll be an important match because 
the tournament is two weeks later.

00:21:48.590 --> 00:21:50.520
I want you all to make sure
you're ready for it!

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:51.280
Yes, sir!

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:54.180
I have one more announcement, but...

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:56.910
Seems changing is taking 
a bit longer than expected.

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:58.500
Why not wait a minute or two?

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.520
"Changing"?

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:00.780
A new guy?

00:22:00.780 --> 00:22:01.750
I wonder who it is.

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:03.760
Sorry for taking so long!

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:10.760
S-Sakura?!

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:15.190
I'd like to introduce the newest 
member of the Mifune Dolphins.

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:17.760
I think a lot of you might already know her.

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:21.200
She's Sakura Takeya's sister. 
He was on the team two years ago.

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:22.550
My name is Sakura Mutsuko.

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.650
It's a pleasure to meet you all!

00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:04.150
I'm going to do my best until I can 
fulfill the promise I made to Hikaru!

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:06.460
Be it framing, throwing, or batting,

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:10.420
with Satou-san in my corner, 
I've got the best coach possible!

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:13.010
At the next training match, 
I'm going to <i>really </i>shine and...

00:24:13.390 --> 00:24:17.220
Hey! Why's Sakura getting coached, too?!

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:20.920
Next time: "Toshiya's Personal Training."

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:25.020
Toshiya's Personal Training

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:23.100
Run to the stage of your dreams!
